      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Successful stent implantation for conduit stenosis has been described; however, this procedure may be complicated by compression of adjacent structures during expansion. We report on a rare case of a single right coronary artery system complicating stent implantation for relief of homograft stenosis in tetralogy of Fallot."},
